<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="641" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Claim terms defined</span></nav><p class="kicker">Reference</p><h1>Property Claim Terms Defined in Plain English</h1><p class="lede">43 terms you’ll meet in policies, estimates and appraisal awards, each explained in a sentence or two. Type in the search box to filter.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="gfilter"><label for="gloss-filter">Search 43 terms</label><input id="gloss-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try “holdback” or “umpire”" autocomplete="off"><p class="hint" data-gcount aria-live="polite"></p></div><div class="az" aria-label="Jump to letter"><a href="#g-A">A</a><a href="#g-B">B</a><a href="#g-C">C</a><a href="#g-D">D</a><a href="#g-E">E</a><a href="#g-H">H</a><a href="#g-I">I</a><a href="#g-L">L</a><a href="#g-M">M</a><a href="#g-O">O</a><a href="#g-P">P</a><a href="#g-R">R</a><a href="#g-S">S</a><a href="#g-U">U</a><a href="#g-W">W</a><a href="#g-X">X</a></div><dl class="glossary"><div class="gterm" id="g-A"><dt>Actual cash value (ACV)</dt><dd>Replacement cost minus depreciation. Often the first payment on a replacement-cost claim.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Additional living expense (ALE)</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs of living elsewhere while your home is being repaired after a covered loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Amount of loss</dt><dd>The dollar value of a covered loss. This is what an appraisal panel decides.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal award</dt><dd>The written decision on the amount of loss, binding once signed by two of the three panel members.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal clause</dt><dd>The policy condition that allows either party to demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraiser</dt><dd>The person each side appoints to value the loss under the appraisal clause.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-B"><dt>Bad faith</dt><dd>A legal claim that an insurer unreasonably handled or denied a claim. Decided by courts, not appraisal panels.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-C"><dt>Coinsurance</dt><dd>A commercial policy clause that can reduce payment if a property is insured for less than a required percentage of its value.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Collapse coverage</dt><dd>Policy language covering the sudden falling-in of a building or part of it, often tied to causes such as the weight of snow or ice.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Contents coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for personal property, often called Coverage C on a homeowners policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Cosmetic damage exclusion</dt><dd>An endorsement that excludes damage affecting only appearance, often applied to metal roofs after hail.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage A</dt><dd>Dwelling coverage on a homeowners policy, the limit for the house itself.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-D"><dt>Declarations page</dt><dd>The summary page of a policy listing coverages, limits, deductibles and endorsements.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Deductible</dt><dd>The portion of a covered loss the policyholder pays before the insurer pays.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Depreciation</dt><dd>The reduction in value due to age, wear or obsolescence, subtracted from replacement cost to find actual cash value.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Direct physical loss</dt><dd>A common trigger phrase in property policies describing tangible damage to property.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Disinterested appraiser</dt><dd>An appraiser with no financial stake in the outcome or the repair work.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Dwelling fire policy</dt><dd>A policy form often used for rental properties, with different terms than a homeowners policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-E"><dt>Extended replacement cost</dt><dd>An endorsement that pays above the dwelling limit, often by a set percentage, if rebuilding costs exceed it.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-H"><dt>Holdback</dt><dd>Recoverable depreciation withheld until repairs are completed.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-I"><dt>Ice dam</dt><dd>A ridge of ice at the eaves that traps meltwater, which can back up under roofing and into the home.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-L"><dt>Line item</dt><dd>A single entry in an estimate describing a task, quantity and price.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Loss of use</dt><dd>Coverage that includes additional living expense and fair rental value after a covered loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-M"><dt>Matching</dt><dd>The issue of whether undamaged materials must be replaced so repairs match in color and style.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Mitigation</dt><dd>Reasonable steps taken after a loss to prevent further damage, such as tarping or water extraction.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-O"><dt>Ordinance or law coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for added costs of bringing a damaged building up to current codes.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Other structures</dt><dd>Coverage for detached structures such as fences, garages and sheds, often called Coverage B.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Overhead and profit (O&amp;P)</dt><dd>A general contractor’s charge for coordinating a job, often 10% overhead and 10% profit.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-P"><dt>Percentage deductible</dt><dd>A deductible calculated as a percentage of the dwelling limit rather than a flat amount.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Proof of loss</dt><dd>A sworn statement of the amount claimed, which insurers may request within a set time.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Public adjuster</dt><dd>A licensed professional who represents a policyholder in negotiating the overall claim.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-R"><dt>Recoverable depreciation</dt><dd>Depreciation that can be paid once repairs or replacement are completed under a replacement-cost policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Replacement cost value (RCV)</dt><dd>The cost to repair or replace damaged property with materials of like kind and quality, without deduction for depreciation.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-S"><dt>Scope of loss</dt><dd>The list of damaged items and the repairs needed. Many disputes are about scope rather than price.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Snow load</dt><dd>The weight of accumulated snow and ice on a roof, measured in pounds per square foot.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Square (roofing)</dt><dd>100 square feet of roof surface.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Subrogation</dt><dd>The insurer’s right to recover what it paid from a third party responsible for the loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Suit limitation clause</dt><dd>Policy language setting the time to file a lawsuit against the insurer.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Supplement</dt><dd>A request to add items or costs to an estimate after the initial review.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Surplus lines insurer</dt><dd>An insurer not licensed in the standard market that can cover hard-to-place risks.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-U"><dt>Umpire</dt><dd>The neutral third panel member who decides items the two appraisers can’t agree on.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-W"><dt>Wildland-urban interface (WUI)</dt><dd>Areas where homes meet or mix with undeveloped wildland vegetation, with higher wildfire risk.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-X"><dt>Xactimate</dt><dd>Estimating software widely used by insurers and contractors to price property repairs.</dd></div></dl></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>A short call tells you whether appraisal fits your claim, or whether something else would serve you better.</p><a class="big-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-y full" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 8am–6pm MT</small></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Resources</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/how-the-appraisal-clause-works/">How the appraisal clause works<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/idaho-appraisal-questions/">Idaho appraisal FAQ<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-terms-defined/" aria-current="page">Claim terms defined<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-know-how/">Appraisal know-how guides<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div>
